{"acceptance_length": 4.352941176470588, "acceptance_lengths": [3, 5, 4, 6, 2, 1, 8, 8, 1, 2, 3, 3, 5, 3, 1, 6, 2, 3, 2, 4, 1, 1, 2, 4, 4, 1, 4, 8, 3, 8, 4, 6, 4, 8, 8, 8, 2, 8, 1, 1, 1, 8, 8, 4, 8, 8, 8, 5, 7, 4, 3], "accepted_draft_lengths": [2, 4, 3, 5, 1, 0, 7, 7, 0, 1, 2, 2, 4, 2, 0, 5, 1, 2, 1, 3, 0, 0, 1, 3, 3, 0, 3, 7, 2, 7, 3, 5, 3, 7, 7, 7, 1, 7, 0, 0, 0, 7, 7, 3, 7, 7, 7, 4, 6, 3, 3], "allocated_memory_after_bytes": 22851417088, "allocated_memory_before_bytes": 22851407872, "benchmark": "mbpp", "completion": "To solve the problem, we need to write a function `noprofit_noloss(cost, selling_price)` that returns `True` if there is **no profit and no loss**, i.e., when the **selling price equals the cost price**. Otherwise, it should return `False`.\n\n### \u2705 Logic:\n- If `selling_price == cost`, then it's a **no profit, no loss** situation \u2192 return `True`\n- Otherwise, return `False`\n\n### \u2705 Code:\n```python\ndef noprofit_noloss(cost, selling_price):\n    return selling_price == cost\n```\n\n### \u2705 Test Cases:\n```python\nassert noprofit_noloss(1500, 1200) == False  # Profit\nassert noprofit_noloss(100, 100) == True    # No profit, no loss\nassert noprofit_noloss(2000, 5000) == False # Loss\n```\n\nThis function satisfies all the given test cases.", "decode_seconds": 2.882617139723152, "draft_calls": 51, "event": "benchmark_row", "input_tokens": 120, "mapper_checkpoint_sha256": "39e658f686a42567902a3965d030f8fed3d6639befa2f9aa766d1ce35ae83e40", "method": "relay_reduced", "output_hash": "5aa76f06b5c864faf8868b672b2c2da66299b6fdd41b3a9bed05a06b2590ef30", "output_tokens": 223, "peak_allocated_memory_bytes": 22965952512, "peak_reserved_memory_bytes": 23358078976, "problem_id": "Mbpp/637", "profile_regions_ms": {"draft": 1187.2281566858292, "prefill_full_target": 45.648094177246094, "prefill_relay": 0.27561599016189575, "relay": 11.49158400297165, "unattributed_runtime": 41.922680642455816, "verification_full_target": 1596.0510082244873}, "prop